// Ch14 side moment (optional, B01, before the vows). The young lamp-bearer from Ch13, in his robe, about to walk. If
// Liss fixed his lamp (ch13_fixed_lamplighter_lamp) he is steady; if not, she sees it lean and fixes it now. Hope, an
// afternoon's worth (the chapter's rule: it must be real so the trap costs). Sets ch14_saw_the_lamplighter.
title: ch14_side_six_lamps
location: ch14/lacquer_court
---
<<if $ch13_fixed_lamplighter_lamp>>
    Townsfolk as "Young lamp-bearer" [smile]: Look. Straight. I'm third in. Watch for me. #line:ch14_lamps_001
    Liss [soft_smile]: I'll be watching. #line:ch14_lamps_002
<<else>>
    Townsfolk as "Young lamp-bearer" [worried]: It's leaning. It's leaning and we go in after the bells. #line:ch14_lamps_003
    Liss [neutral]: Hold still. Cracked wick-seat. There. #line:ch14_lamps_004
    Townsfolk as "Young lamp-bearer" [surprised]: Oh. Oh, thank you. #line:ch14_lamps_005
<<endif>>
Liss [tender]: Tobin's going to cry when the lamps come in. He cries at everything. Don't tell him I said. #line:ch14_lamps_006
<<set $ch14_saw_the_lamplighter = true>>
===
